  "notes": "West leads the ♥5 against 6♠. An honour is played from North and East's ♥A should be ruffed with a middle trump.\n\nSouth should cash 2 top spades. If West has 3 spades he may try to unblock his high spades, but South's carefully preserved ♠2 will still endplay him.\n\nWest has only diamonds and clubs left. Returning either suit will not only take away South's loser in that suit, but will also provide an entry to dummy. North's heart winner will take care of South's other minor suit loser.\n\nIf spades prove to be 2-2, after drawing trump, South should cash a top winner in both diamonds and clubs. If neither Queen drops, South should play West for both the ♦Q and ♣Q. West will be strip squeezed on the run of the trumps.\n\nOn the last trump West will have to either come down to a singleton Queen or expose himself to an endplay. South will have to guess West's remaining distribution in order to make the contract.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥5 against 6♠. An honour is played from North and East's ♥A should be ruffed with a middle trump.",
    "South should cash 2 top spades. If West has 3 spades he may try to unblock his high spades, but South's carefully preserved ♠2 will still endplay him.",
    "West has only diamonds and clubs left. Returning either suit will not only take away South's loser in that suit, but will also provide an entry to dummy. North's heart winner will take care of South's other minor suit loser.",
    "If spades prove to be 2-2, after drawing trump, South should cash a top winner in both diamonds and clubs. If neither Queen drops, South should play West for both the ♦Q and ♣Q. West will be strip squeezed on the run of the trumps.",
    "On the last trump West will have to either come down to a singleton Queen or expose himself to an endplay. South will have to guess West's remaining distribution in order to make the contract."
